# Eval worker image for RoboLab cases (dimos.evals.suites.robolab): the dimos eval stack
# with NVIDIA RoboLab beside it, in its own Python. One container runs one case: RoboLab's
# runner and dimos, side by side.
#
# RoboLab's checkout and assets come from RoboLab's own image. Build that first, from a
# RoboLab v0.3.3 checkout with its LFS assets:
#     docker build -t robolab:0.3.3 -f docker/Dockerfile .
# then, from the dimos repo root:
#     docker build -t dimos-evals:robolab -f docker/evals/Dockerfile.robolab \
#         --build-arg ROBOLAB_IMAGE=robolab:0.3.3 .
#
# Ubuntu 24.04: the dimos agent's HTTP/3 add-on needs glibc 2.38, newer than RoboLab's own
# image (22.04), and Isaac Sim 5.0 supports 24.04.
ARG ROBOLAB_IMAGE=robolab:0.3.3
FROM ${ROBOLAB_IMAGE} AS robolab

FROM ubuntu:24.04

ARG DENO_VERSION=v2.9.8
ARG PYTHON_VERSION=3.12
# The dimos agent needs Node 24 or 26.
ARG NODE_MAJOR=24

ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
# dimos's runtime libraries (lcm needs GLib), and the ones Isaac Sim loads (GLU, X11, Vulkan).
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
    ca-certificates curl wget git unzip build-essential pkg-config \
    libgl1 libegl1 libopengl0 libturbojpeg0-dev portaudio19-dev libusb-1.0-0 iproute2 \
    libglu1-mesa libxt6 libsm6 libice6 libxrender1 libxi6 libxrandr2 libxkbcommon0 \
    libvulkan1 \
    libglib2.0-0t64 libatk1.0-0 libatk-bridge2.0-0 libcairo2 libcups2 libgbm1 \
    libpango-1.0-0 libxcomposite1 libxdamage1 libxkbcommon-x11-0 libnss3 libnspr4 \
    libasound2t64 libatspi2.0-0 libxfixes3 libdrm2 libx11-xcb1 libxext6 libxshmfence1 \
    fonts-liberation \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# The NVIDIA runtime mounts the driver's graphics libraries (NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=all);
# Vulkan finds them only through this ICD file, and EGL through the vendor file.
ENV NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=all
RUN mkdir -p /etc/vulkan/icd.d /usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d \
    && echo '{"file_format_version": "1.0.0", "ICD": {"library_path": "libGLX_nvidia.so.0", "api_version": "1.3.194"}}' \
        > /etc/vulkan/icd.d/nvidia_icd.json \
    && echo '{"file_format_version": "1.0.0", "ICD": {"library_path": "libEGL_nvidia.so.0"}}' \
        > /usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/10_nvidia.json

ENV XDG_CACHE_HOME=/cache \
    XDG_STATE_HOME=/state \
    XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/config \
    DENO_DIR=/cache/deno

RUN curl -fsSL "https://github.com/denoland/deno/releases/download/${DENO_VERSION}/deno-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.zip" \
        -o /tmp/deno.zip \
    && unzip -q /tmp/deno.zip -d /usr/local/bin && rm /tmp/deno.zip \
    && chmod +x /usr/local/bin/deno

RUN curl -fsSL "https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_${NODE_MAJOR}.x" | bash - \
    && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends nodejs \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* /root/.npm

RUN curl -LsSf https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sh
ENV PATH="/root/.local/bin:${PATH}"

# RoboLab: its checkout and assets, and its Isaac Sim 5.0 environment (Python 3.11), with
# what the dimos runner imports (zenoh, msgpack).
COPY --from=robolab /workspace/robolab /opt/robolab
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
    cd /opt/robolab \
    && uv venv --python 3.11 \
    && uv sync --frozen --extra isaac50 \
    && uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python eclipse-zenoh==1.10.1 msgpack==1.1.2

WORKDIR /app

# Dependencies first so code edits don't invalidate the deps layer.
COPY pyproject.toml uv.lock README.md setup.py ./
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
    uv python install "${PYTHON_VERSION}" \
    && uv sync --frozen --no-install-project --python "${PYTHON_VERSION}" \
        --group tests-self-hosted

# GraspGenX's own environment, where its module looks for it (isolated_python_environment),
# so a run starts without installing torch.
COPY native/python/graspgenx native/python/graspgenx
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
    key=$(printf %s /app/native/python/graspgenx | sha256sum | cut -c1-16) \
    && cd native/python/graspgenx \
    && UV_CACHE_DIR=/root/.cache/uv UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=/cache/dimos/isolated-python/$key/.venv \
        uv sync --frozen

COPY . /app
RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
    uv sync --frozen --python "${PYTHON_VERSION}" --group tests-self-hosted \
    && uv run python setup.py build_ext --inplace

# The dimos agent's npm install and build, so its preflight does nothing at run time.
RUN /app/.venv/bin/dimos agent version
# The relay the dimos agent's harness starts, its modules fetched (see relay_run_cmd).
RUN deno cache --frozen --node-modules-dir=none --config web/deno.json web/relay/main.ts

ENV PATH="/app/.venv/bin:${PATH}" \
    VIEWER=none \
    PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1 \
    OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=YES \
    ACCEPT_EULA=Y \
    ROBOLAB_PYTHON=/opt/robolab/.venv/bin/python \
    ROBOLAB_DIR=/opt/robolab

RUN mkdir -p /state /config

COPY docker/evals/entrypoint.sh /entrypoint.sh
ENTRYPOINT ["/entrypoint.sh"]
CMD ["bash"]
